//! run
//! flags: -I ../../src/fort -I support
//! stdout:
//| summary prefix clear ok
/// Holds the verdicts of the prefix clear of the summary solver (D17.7, D17.14, D17.15, D17.18;
/// spec/fir.md 14.1). A zero store or a whole move at a caller path replaces each path below
/// it. An earlier release, owner store or null store at such a path keeps its contents in a
/// private flow slot. A zero store first writes an empty owner into that slot, and the write
/// checks the old owner. It keeps the entry value of a by-value owner parameter: a store over
/// that value is a caller requirement (D17.18), and each caller checks the summary effect of
/// the store. A whole move moves the contents of that slot with the value.
///
/// Each body has one expected verdict:
/// - L: a faulty body that the summary solver fails, and that the calls_heap row does not prove.
/// - F: a faulty body. Neither the summary solver nor the calls_heap row proves it.
/// - K: a valid body that the summary solver proves.
/// - V: a valid body that the summary solver does not prove. It reports no violation.
/// The groups `prefix_clears` and `stored_owner_callers` are the probes of that name in
/// `test/ownership/probes` without their `main`. In the group `by_value` a by-value owner
/// parameter gives the owner that a zero store replaces: each body is valid under the caller
/// requirement that the parameter is null, and the summary solver proves each that it proved on
/// d9595ac4. `test/ownership/probes/by_value_callers.ft` holds faulty callers of 4 of them. In
/// the group `aliases` two inputs name one storage (D17.4).
import ownership_gate_env;
import ownership_recursive_env;
import ownership_source_calls_env;

